'''Darkmadillo''' (クロマジロ, ''Kuromajiro'', '''Kuromadillo''') is a [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark]] enemy that appears in [[Zero Legends]]. It was added in [[Version 14.7 Update|Version 14.7]].

{{Enemy Info
|name = Darkmadillo
|image = E 745.png
|first appearance = '''ZL''': [[Lying Somniloquy|Sub-chapter 24 - Lying Somniloquy]]
|money drop = 550¢ - 2,172¢
}}

==Enemy==
This armadillo is essentially a weaker [[Tackey]], filling a more supportive role to chip away at your weaker units such as [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]] and [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]]. Darkmadillo has a low standing range, and its [[Long Distance]] attacks pierce up to 500 while having a near non-existent blind spot, which gives it an expansive effective range that covers a surprising amount of the field. This does make it vulnerable to attacks though, so take advantage of that!

==Strategy==
You don't want many Darkmadillos stacking up; while weak on their own, their damage stacks up exponentially, especially given their high magnifications. As such, rushing is the optimal strategy, since Bombercat's range is too long for him to enter Darkmadillo's blind spot. Use [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]],[[Talents|Talented]] [[Cats in a Box (Special Cat)|Heavy Assault C.A.T.]], among others, to infiltrate this menace's blind spot and strike it into the enemy goal.

